Received: " ```html <ocelle-status-indicator tone="success" label="Running" pulse></ocelle-status-indicator> <ocelle-status-indicator tone="warning"></ocelle-status-indicator> Blocked ``` `ocelle-status-indicator` is a status dot: a solid circle in the colour of its `tone`, `info`, `success`, `warning`, `danger` or `neutral` (the default). The dot is `--ocelle-size-indicator` (8 px) square, round with the pill radius, and never transparent, empty or only outlined. An absent, empty or unknown `tone` shows `neutral`; the attribute keeps the value as written and the `tone` property reads `"neutral"`. Setting the property writes the attribute as given. `ocelle-status-indicator` emits no event and adds no tab stop. **Naming.** Without a `label` the indicator is hidden from the accessibility tree: place text naming the state next to it, since a state is never shown by colour alone. `label` is the one way to name the indicator: with a non-empty `label` it is one image with that name. A host `aria-label` is not supported, and the indicator does not read it. The label is trimmed, and an empty or whitespace-only label counts as none. The indicator is not a busy or progress signal: it sets no `aria-busy` and no live region. For progress, use `ocelle-progress`. **Pulse.** With `pulse`, a ring around the dot grows and fades three times, each `--ocelle-motion-pulse` long (4.8 s by default), and then only the solid dot is shown; the dot itself never fades, moves or changes size. The pulse ends by itself within 5 s (WCAG 2.2.2) and does not come back while `pulse` stays set. A host that overrides `--ocelle-motion-pulse` keeps the token's value times three, the fixed iteration count, at or below 5 s: at most `1666ms`. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` no animation runs, with or without `pulse`, and the dot is shown solid; a change to `reduce` stops a run at once, and the change back starts one. **When a run starts.** A run starts when `pulse` is set on a rendered indicator, when the indicator is connected with `pulse` set, when it is shown again with `pulse` set, and when reduced motion ends; nothing else starts or restarts it, not a change of `tone`, `label`, the theme, its size or position, `visibility` or opacity, nor scrolling it out of view and back. Each connection, and each time the indicator is shown again after `display: none` or `hidden`, starts a run, so a host that re-inserts, moves, re-renders or re-shows an indicator more often than every 5 s keeps it pulsing: keep `pulse` off between changes, or keep the element in place. Removing `pulse` and setting it again within one task starts no run; set it again in a later task. A state-preserving move (`moveBefore()`) and a reveal from `hidden="until-found"` start no run. Opening a `<details>` around a pulsing indicator starts no run: a run under way when it closed goes on while it is closed and may end unseen. **Forced colours.** In forced colours the dot is drawn in `CanvasText`, and so is the ring, so it stays visible on the system background. **Tokens.** `ocelle-status-indicator` reads the tokens `--ocelle-color-info`, `--ocelle-color-success`, `--ocelle-color-warning`, `--ocelle-color-danger`, `--ocelle-color-neutral`, `--ocelle-size-indicator`, `--ocelle-radius-pill`, `--ocelle-border-width`, `--ocelle-motion-pulse` and `--ocelle-easing-standard`. "

