Received: " ```html <ocelle-pill-tag status="warning">Blocked</ocelle-pill-tag> <ocelle-pill-tag variant="badge" density="compact">3</ocelle-pill-tag> <ocelle-pill-tag interactive status="info" aria-pressed="true">Mine</ocelle-pill-tag> <ocelle-pill-tag href="/missions?state=blocked" status="warning">Blocked</ocelle-pill-tag> ``` `ocelle-pill-tag` is a state pill or a count badge: `<ocelle-pill-tag status="warning">Blocked</ocelle-pill-tag>`, `<ocelle-pill-tag variant="badge">3</ocelle-pill-tag>`. `status` is one of `info`, `success`, `warning`, `danger` and `neutral` (the default); an absent, empty or unknown `status` shows `neutral`, the attribute keeps the value as written and the `status` property reads `"neutral"`. The vocabulary and its colour pairs are those of the notice's tone; the default is the pill's own. **Looks.** `variant="pill"`, the default, fills the pill with `--ocelle-color-<status>-bg` and sets its text in `--ocelle-color-<status>`; `variant="badge"` has no fill, a `--ocelle-border-width` border in `--ocelle-color-<status>` and its text in tabular figures (`--ocelle-figures`); both are set in Schibsted Grotesk (`--ocelle-font-sans`), never in a monospace family. Every `ocelle-pill-tag`, in either variant and in every mode, a count badge and a filter toggle included, is a state pill, so its corners take `--ocelle-radius-pill`. In forced colours the pill and the badge keep a visible border. The status colours are checked for contrast on the main grounds; a badge placed on a state ground (inside a notice, say) is outside that check. **Densities.** `density="compact"` sets the text in `--ocelle-font-size-xs` at `--ocelle-line-height-snug` (1.2), with a block padding of exactly `--ocelle-space-1` and an inline padding of `--ocelle-space-2`; the default density sets it in `--ocelle-font-size-sm` at `--ocelle-line-height-tight`, padded `--ocelle-space-1` and `--ocelle-space-3`. An unknown `variant` or `density` shows the default and stays in the attribute as written. **Content.** The default slot holds the text; the `icon` slot takes one decorative icon before the text, one line tall, following the slot convention, so a pill has the same height with and without an icon. A pill with no text renders an empty pill. The part `pill` (the visual box) can be styled with `::part()`. **A static pill.** A static pill, one with neither `interactive` nor a link `href`, is not focusable, has no role of its own and exposes its text as plain text; a click on it reaches the elements around it as a click on its text would (an enclosing link follows, a focusable ancestor takes focus). A static pill wraps a text that does not fit onto further lines; it never truncates it. `label` and `disabled` have no effect on a static pill. `title` and ARIA attributes on a static pill stay on the element as written; the element does not move or change them, and `title` keeps the browser's own tooltip. ARIA states and names on a static pill (`aria-pressed`, `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby` and the others) stay on an element with no role, where axe may report them: remove them (`removeAttribute`) once a pill is static, or clear them before making it static. An `href` that is empty, whitespace only, does not parse as a URL or is a `javascript:` URL is no link: the pill stays static. The interactive pill, with `interactive` or a link `href`, is described below. **Layout.** In a flex row a static pill is not shrunk below its longest word, so a one-word pill such as "Blocked" stays on one line beside a long name; a host that wants it to shrink further sets `min-inline-size: 0` on it, and its words then break inside the pill. A static pill's longest word is capped at its container's whole inline size, beyond which it breaks inside the pill; beside a sibling in a flex row such a word can make the row overflow by the sibling's width, unless the host sets `min-inline-size: 0` on the pill. In a grid track or a flex column that stretches its items a short static pill keeps the width of its text; only its host is stretched. A one-line pill sits on the baseline of the text around it, inline in text and in a flex row aligned by baseline, with and without an icon; a pill that wraps fills its line, its first line on that line's baseline. `ocelle-pill-tag` reads the tokens `--ocelle-color-<status>` and `--ocelle-color-<status>-bg` of the five statuses, `--ocelle-border-width`, `--ocelle-radius-pill`, `--ocelle-font-sans`, `--ocelle-figures`, `--ocelle-font-size-sm`, `--ocelle-font-size-xs`, `--ocelle-line-height-tight`, `--ocelle-line-height-snug`, `--ocelle-space-1`, `--ocelle-space-2` and `--ocelle-space-3`. A static pill emits no event of its own. **An interactive pill.** With `interactive` the pill is a toggle or filter button, one native `<button type="button">` in its shadow root: `<ocelle-pill-tag interactive status="info" aria-pressed="true">Mine</ocelle-pill-tag>`. With an `href` that is a link (not empty, not whitespace only, parsed as a URL and not a `javascript:` URL) the pill is one native `<a>` with that `href`, whether or not `interactive` is set: `<ocelle-pill-tag href="/missions?state=blocked" status="warning">Blocked</ocelle-pill-tag>`. The element itself is never focusable and has no role; the inner control is its one tab stop, and the element's `focus()` and `click()` reach it. The part `control` is the inner `<button>` or `<a>` of an interactive pill, which is also its `pill` part. The control conventions it follows are those of `ocelle-button` (see Control conventions). **Passthrough and names.** `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby`, `aria-controls`, `aria-current`, `aria-pressed` and `title` set on an interactive pill are moved to the inner control, each with an element-owned `data-ocelle-moved-*` mirror, as on `ocelle-button`; `aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby` and `aria-controls` name elements by id in the element's own tree. The inner control is named by `aria-labelledby`, then `aria-label`, then `label` (trimmed; empty or whitespace only counts as none), then the pill's text. An interactive pill with no text (an icon only, or nothing) has no accessible name of its own: name it with `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby` or `label`; the element does not invent a name, and axe reports an unnamed one. Do not set `title` on an interactive pill: it is moved to the inner control as the browser's own tooltip and description. **Activation.** Each activation of an enabled interactive pill (a pointer click, Enter, Space in button mode, the element's `click()`) dispatches `ocelle-pill-tag-activate` from the element (`bubbles`, `composed`, `cancelable`, `detail` `{}`) before its `click` reaches any bubble-phase listener on the element or its ancestors. Calling `preventDefault()` on `ocelle-pill-tag-activate` cancels the click's default action: a link does not navigate, and a button still delivers its `click`, with `defaultPrevented` true. A link-mode click with Ctrl, Meta, Shift or Alt held delivers its `click` and no `ocelle-pill-tag-activate`, and the browser's own handling of the modifier applies; a middle click dispatches neither; a disabled or static pill dispatches no `ocelle-pill-tag-activate`. `disabled` takes an interactive pill out of the tab order, reports it disabled and stops every activation; a disabled link has no `href`. **States.** `:state(pressed)` matches a button-mode pill whose moved `aria-pressed` is `"true"`, which also gives the pressed look; `"false"`, `"mixed"` and any other value reach the button as written with neither. `aria-pressed` has no effect on a link: on a link-mode pill it is moved and mirrored but not applied, and gives no `:state(pressed)`; it applies again if the pill returns to button mode. `:state(current)` matches an interactive pill whose moved `aria-current` is set to anything but `"false"`; it draws no mark of its own. **Interactive looks.** An interactive pill has a `--ocelle-color-accent-strong` border on its status ground (a badge keeps its status-colour border); hover takes the status colour on a pill's border and the status ground as a badge's fill; pressing and the pressed state add an inset `--ocelle-bar-width` cue in the status colour; no state changes the pill's box. A disabled interactive pill is set in `--ocelle-color-disabled-ink` on `--ocelle-color-disabled-bg`, border included, whatever its status and variant. In forced colours a pressed pill fills with `Highlight` and sets its text in `HighlightText`, so it stays distinct from an unpressed one, and a disabled pill is `GrayText`. Keyboard focus shows the token focus ring on the inner control (`--ocelle-focus-width`, `--ocelle-focus-offset`, `--ocelle-color-focus`). An interactive pill is at least `--ocelle-target-small` (24 px) in block size and in inline size in either density, whatever its text and its font size; in `compact` density its block padding is then at least `--ocelle-space-1`. An interactive pill keeps one focus-ring extent (`--ocelle-focus-offset` plus `--ocelle-focus-width`, 5 px) of inline margin on each side and caps its inline size at its container's less two such extents, so its ring stays inside a container that clips; a container that clips in the block direction keeps that much unclipped space above and below it. **Changing the mode.** The mode follows `interactive` and `href` whenever either changes: when a pill becomes static each moved attribute is written back to the element with the value it last had (an off value such as `aria-pressed="false"` included) and its mirror removed; when it becomes interactive they are moved again; a switch between button and link mode keeps them moved. A static pill that carries `data-ocelle-moved-*` mirrors when it upgrades (copied markup) writes each back as its attribute, unless the element already sets that attribute, and removes the mirror. If the inner control has focus when a pill switches between button and link mode, the new inner control has focus afterwards, with the focus ring only if it showed before; a pill made static while its inner control has focus loses focus as a removed element does, so move focus yourself before making a focused pill static; a pill that becomes interactive does not take focus. ARIA states written back to a pill made static (such as `aria-pressed`) stay on an element with no role: clear them (`removeAttribute`) once the pill is static, or before making it static. **Truncation and the full text.** An enabled interactive pill shows its text on one line; a text that does not fit is truncated with an ellipsis at the inline end, and `ocelle-tooltip` shows the full text (the default slot's text, trimmed and with its whitespace collapsed) on hover and on keyboard focus, with the tooltip's own delay, persistence and Escape. The inner control's accessible name stays the full text, or the name `aria-labelledby`, `aria-label` or `label` gives it, and the tooltip adds nothing to the accessibility tree. A pill whose text fits shows no tooltip; truncation follows the pill's inline size, its text and `disabled` whenever they change. A disabled interactive pill is never truncated: it wraps its text onto further lines inside the pill, breaking a long word anywhere, and shows no tooltip. Truncation needs a definite inline size: a flex or grid parent, a fixed table layout, or a cell or column width; in an auto-layout table cell the pill grows to its text instead. In a flex row a truncating pill shares the shrink with its siblings by their flex bases, so a sibling such as a mission name shrinks too, down to its longest word: give the sibling `flex: none` (or `flex-shrink: 0`) to keep its size. `flex: 1 1 0` on the pill also keeps the sibling's size, but it stretches the pill's visible box to the whole room left, a fitting pill included, since the inner control fills its host. On a touch screen a truncated pill shows no tooltip, as `ocelle-tooltip` shows none for touch; its full text stays its access